# onnxruntime-node's postinstall downloads the CUDA 12 execution-provider
# binaries from a Microsoft NuGet CDN. The 1.24.x copy (pulled in by
# @huggingface/transformers for the CLIP/vision worker) requests that manifest
# UNCONDITIONALLY on linux/x64 — no GPU detection — so a CPU-only box still
# reaches out, and a blocked or slow egress path fails `npm ci` outright with
# ETIMEDOUT. The CPU runtime is bundled in the package; only the GPU EP is
# fetched. Two keys because 1.21 (our pinned root) reads the deprecated *_cuda
# name and 1.24 reads the new one.
#
# This lives HERE, not in canvas-server: since inference became its own process
# canvas-server has no inference dependency at all, so this is the only tree
# that can hit the download.
#
# Drop these on a GPU box that should actually use the CUDA EP.
onnxruntime-node-install=skip
onnxruntime-node-install-cuda=skip
